  "topic_en": "Gauss computes the constant parts P and Q of $(1-\\frac{H}{F}\\cos w)^{-3/2}$ and $\\cos w\\,(1-\\frac{H}{F}\\cos w)^{-3/2}$ using the arithmetic-geometric mean, works a numerical example in logarithms, and then sets up formulas for M, N cos n and N sin n (fifth step, apparently of a secular perturbation computation).",
  "transcription": "85.\nViertes Moment. Bestimmung der constanten Theile von\n$\\frac{1}{(1-\\frac{H}{F}\\cos w)^{\\frac32}}$ und $\\frac{\\cos w}{(1-\\frac{H}{F}\\cos w)^{\\frac32}}$\ndie wir durch P, Q bezeichnen.\nEs sei $a = \\sqrt{(1+\\frac{H}{F})}$ $b=\\sqrt{(1-\\frac{H}{F})}$ $c'=\\frac{H}{8F}$\n$a' = \\frac12(a+b)$ $b'=\\sqrt{ab}$ $c''=\\frac{c'c'}{a'a'}$\n$a''=\\frac12(a'+b')$ $b''=\\sqrt{a'b'}$ $c'''=\\frac{c''c''}{a''a''}$\nu. s. w.\n$a^\\infty = b^\\infty = \\alpha$ [-so wird-] $\\frac{1}{c'}(2c''+4c'''+8c^{IV}+\\text{etc.}) = u$\n$P=\\frac{1-u.\\frac{H}{F}}{\\alpha(1-\\frac{HH}{FF})}$ $Q=\\frac{\\frac{H}{F}-u}{\\alpha(1-\\frac{HH}{FF})}$\nMan kann ein für allemal eine Tafel construiren welche für das Argument $\\frac{H}{F}$ die Grössen P und Q giebt.\nAnwendung auf unser Beispiel\n9.5209417\n1.1013744\n$\\frac{H}{F}$ ...... 9.4195673 0,26276488 $1+\\frac{H}{F}$ ... 0.1013225 $1-\\frac{H}{F}$ ...... 9.8676060\na .... 1,1237281[?] 0.0506612\nb ....... 0,8586239 9.9338030 c' 8.5164773 $2\\frac{c''}{c'}$ ... 8.8252059 0.06686609\na' ...... 0.9911760 9.9961507 8.5203266\nb' ..... 0.9822728 9.9922321 c'' 7.0406532 $4\\frac{c'''}{c'}$ .... 6.1784975 0,00015 0833\na'' ...... 0.9867244 9.9941958 7.0464574 $8\\frac{c^{IV}}{c'}$ ... 0.5840551\nb'' ...... 0.9867143 9.9941914 c''' 4.0929148 u = 0.06701692\n$\\alpha$ ...... 0.9867193 9.9941936 4.0987212 $\\frac{H}{F}$ = 0.26276488\nc$^{IV}$ 8.1974424 9.2916973\nu ....... 8.8261845 9.9941936\nH:F ...... 9.4195673 9.2975037\n0.01760692 9.6689285\n9.9922840 Q ...... 9.3285752\n9.9631221\nP ......... 0.0291619\nFünftes Moment. Man setze\n$M = \\frac{\\tang\\zeta\\sqrt{(1-\\tang\\zeta^2)}}{F^{\\frac32}}\\{{+P\\cot\\zeta+}Pe'\\cos\\varphi + \\frac12 K(P\\cos k - Q\\cos(h+k))\\}$\n$N\\cos n = \\frac{\\sqrt{(1-\\tang\\zeta^2)}}{F^{\\frac32}}\\{{+-P\\tang\\zeta+}(-Pe'\\cos\\varphi\\tang\\zeta^2 - \\frac12 K(P\\cos k - Q\\cos(h+k))\\}$\n$N\\sin n = \\frac{K(1-\\tang\\zeta^2)}{2F^{\\frac32}}\\{-P\\sin k [-+-] Q\\sin(h+k)\\}$",
